{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476247-imposing-exalted-sorcery-cosmology-as-an-awakened-paradigm","id":1476247,"title":"Imposing Exalted Sorcery/Cosmology as an Awakened Paradigm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-11T18:35:13-08:00","id":1476247,"title":"Imposing Exalted Sorcery/Cosmology as an Awakened Paradigm","content":"Suppose a newly Awakened Mage discovers just how fluid reality really is, and decides to impose his own based on a (possibly non-existent) TTRPG. Best as I can extrapolate it, this is a sort of like believing that &quot;Everything is Chaos/Data/Illusion&quot; to create effects based on the idea of &quot;Divine Order, Earthly Chaos&quot;. He doesn't really believe in the Unconquered Sun and Five Elemental Dragons (apologies to the Asian Technocrats), but he fakes it well enough for it not to matter.<br /> <br /> Put another way, the mage sees the universe as infinite monkeys at infinite typewriters, and while it may not be Shakespear he slips his own story into the presses when they're not looking<br /> <br /> So, my question: Does anyone else think this makes enough sense to hold up in game?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T19:10:13-08:00","id":1476248,"title":"","content":"So: you're asking if a mage can use a Focus that he doesn't believe in. The short answer is: No. M20 makes a point that belief is what fuels awakened magick. If the character doesn't actually believe it, there's nothing to fuel it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-11-2022, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T20:44:54-08:00","id":1476252,"title":"","content":"I can see a Marauder making something like this work if their particular madness happens to correspond to the Exalted setting, but not a mage who doesn't believe in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T20:57:39-08:00","id":1476253,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't even need to be a Marauder. However, there would likely have to be some Quiet involved. That inclines it towards Maraudership, but doesn't mandate it.<br /> <br /> To be clear, my point of contention with the idea isn't how outlandish it is. As Matt just pointed out, there are mages who have some very outlandish Paradigms. The point of contention lies entirely in the realm of \u201che doesn't actually believe it\u201d.<br /> <br /> Heck, take out the \u201che read it in a role-playing book\u201d part, and you don't even need any Quiet: there were hints provided at one point that Exalted was the prehistory of the World of Darkness; and those hints have never officially been rescinded. So a mage who digs up evidence of that prehistory (real or not; it just needs to be believable) could conceivably take the notion of Exalted cosmology dead serious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-12-2022, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T23:11:57-08:00","id":1476262,"title":"","content":"In addition to needing to believe, one of the reasons Focuses tend to be a lot more coherent than this, is because magic is a lot easier when you have a whole belief structure around how it works.<br /> <br /> Mages that learn, in theory, how fluid reality is, and just try to make things happen can look forward to failing, or worse, a lot. Without the full scaffolding of a paradigm, practice, and instruments translating theory into practical know-how, hello 1 WP just to roll and a +3 difficulty mod on top of it; assuming it doesn't just fizzle out from your lack of study of Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T05:25:43-07:00","id":1476376,"title":"","content":"To throw a bone at the idea: A mage can use something he know it's a fiction as a <i>Tool</i>, but not as the basis of <i>Paradigm/Belief/Practice. </i><br /> <br /> Take a look at Chaos Magick, for instance, both in the books and real life. Chaos magicians will dress and summon the power of pulp figures, like Dr. Strange, not because they believe these are &quot;real people&quot; (in a conventional sense), but because they believe these are symbols that have power<br /> <br /> This is different from believing you're Dr. Strange, or in the Marvel Universe. A Chaos Magician would recognize the power in other symbols, and be cappable on tapping on other close symbolic tools, like impersonating other comic book characters and such. Only a mage in Silence would be &quot;stuck&quot; in another reality or character, that on some level he knows it's false.<br /> <br /> SO, &quot;He doesn't really believe in the Unconquered Sun and Five Elemental Dragons (apologies to the Asian Technocrats), but he fakes it well enough for it not to matter.&quot;. That <i>could </i>be describing a mage that uses Exalted, and it's heroic narrative, as a one of it's Tools to &quot;cheat&quot; reality. But it shouldn't be the whole of the Paradigm, or even the whole basis of a Practice.<br /> <br /> In Essence: You need to <i>determine what he <b>does </b>believe in, </i>to have a working Focus. A mage could be a conman so good that can cheat reality, but it would be a mage that <i>believes </i>in the power of such deceptions. That belief needs to be fleshed out, that's what the different steps of the Focus are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-14-2022, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}